              "name": "The Blond Beast",
              "subtitle": "The predator beneath aristocratic morality",
              "body": "Nietzsche's provocative image, in the First Essay, for the magnificent, terrifying animal vigor that lies at the core of every aristocratic race — the thing one is right to fear even as its bouts of savagery alternate with feats of art, friendship, and heroism."
